{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And He said to him, etc. Wherefore, etc. Behold, etc.</b> One needs to know what argument this is — ״עַל מָה״ (wherefore) and so on — concerning his evil conduct! Further, what argument is there in the statement ״הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי״ (behold, I), since he did not know, as the verse testifies: ״וַיְגַל ה׳ אֶת עֵינֵי בִלְעָם״ — from this you learn that his eyes had been closed until now. Or perhaps HaShem intended to humble his pride so that he would acknowledge with his own mouth and say that the she-ass saw the angel three times while he did not see, and from this would also be revealed the extent of his diminished perception of hidden things. Therefore He said to him ״עַל מָה״ and concluded by saying <b>הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי</b> etc. <b>וַתִּרְאַנִי הָאָתוֹן</b>. Here He thrust an arrow into his heart, for he was forced to say with his own mouth that he had eyes yet could not see, as the she-ass saw — as he said: ״לֹא יָדַעְתִּי כִּי אַתָּה נִצָּב לִקְרָאתִי״, and this was the ultimate intent in the angel's words." "<b>Further,</b> He intended in this to remind him of what this journey had caused him, on the principle of their statement, of blessed memory (Sanhedrin 106a), that Balaam at first had access to ruach ha-kodesh, and when he joined himself to Balak it departed from him and he was called a diviner (Joshua 13:22). And this is what He reminded him of — that he did not know the angel standing before him, which had not been the case previously, when he would see by ruach ha-kodesh. And the reason for the angel's going out to meet him, He informed him in the statement <b>כִּי יָרַט הַדֶּרֶךְ</b> etc., meaning 'the way was contrary,' as Ramban explained, and the meaning of 'the way' — Balaam's own path upon which he had been walking."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads ה׳ (abbreviation for the divine name); rendered as HaShem per the standard convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:49.285575699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}